# nr-office-fonts: the new crate mixdog-fonts (font faces, system font discovery, CSS font matching, HarfBuzz-equal shaping, canvas measureText, font provisioning).

## native/core/Cargo.toml

[workspace] members: add, after "crates/mixdog-fsio" (any place in the list):

    "crates/mixdog-fonts",

[workspace.dependencies]: add, next to `mixdog-fsio = { path = "crates/mixdog-fsio" }`:

    mixdog-fonts = { path = "crates/mixdog-fonts" }

[workspace.dependencies]: add (owner decision "font parsing and shaping"; every crate below is in the local cargo cache; default
features of ttf-parser are kept: the crate reads variation axes and name strings, which need "variable-fonts" and "std"):

    ttf-parser = "=0.25.1"
    rustybuzz = "=0.20.1"
    unicode-script = "0.5"

unicode-script: the cache holds 0.5.9 (the plan said 0.5.7); rustybuzz needs >= 0.5.2, so one version serves both.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

New packages (all sources are in the cache; regenerate offline with `cargo update -w`, no other package changes):
  mixdog-fonts          deps: mixdog-fsio, mixdog-workspace-hack, rustybuzz, sha2, ttf-parser, unicode-script (dev: mixdog-office-base, serde_json)
  ttf-parser 0.25.1
  rustybuzz 0.20.1      deps: bitflags 2.x, bytemuck 1.x, core_maths 0.1.1, log, smallvec 1.x, ttf-parser, unicode-bidi-mirroring 0.4.0,
                        unicode-ccc 0.4.0, unicode-properties (already locked), unicode-script
  core_maths 0.1.1      dep: libm 0.2.x (cached 0.2.16)
  unicode-bidi-mirroring 0.4.0, unicode-ccc 0.4.0, unicode-script 0.5.9
rustybuzz's `wasm-shaper` feature (the only user of wasmi, which is not cached) is off by default and stays off.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the repository's hakari check after adding the member; take its output if it asks for a line (ttf-parser, rustybuzz and unicode-script
may be added to the hack's dependency list).

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.

## Consumers (later tasks)

The tasks that depend on this crate (the text-metrics port, the PDF font and embed tasks, the raster canvas) read these entry points:
  mixdog_fonts::css_font::parse(&str) -> ParsedFont           the ctx.font shorthand
  mixdog_fonts::measure::{measure_text, measure_parsed, faces_of}   measureText; the proof argument is a lane ReadProof
  mixdog_fonts::registry::Registry                            families(), family(name), register_file(proof, path, alias), register_dir(proof, dir)
  mixdog_fonts::discovery::{Catalog, scan, HostEnv}           the machine's fonts, scanned lazily once; Catalog::scan(proof, env) -> Arc<Scan>
  mixdog_fonts::provision::{NOTO_FONTS, FontDef, verify, installed_path, register_installed, mac_office_font_dir}
  mixdog_fonts::shape::{runs, hb_face, shape_run, shape}      rustybuzz shaping per script run
  mixdog_fonts::Face                                          names, style, metrics, axes, named instances, glyph coverage, load_all (ttc)

## Follow-up for the owner of native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/domain_seams/office_fonts.rs (not edited here)

That file holds its own copy of the pinned Noto table (FontDef, NOTO_FONTS, url(), verify). Once mixdog-fonts is a workspace member it can
depend on it (edge mixdog-app-server-daemon -> mixdog-fonts) and re-export mixdog_fonts::provision::{FontDef, NOTO_FONTS, verify}, keeping
only the download, the OS registration and the install steps; the table, its digests and the verify messages are the same text.

## Fixtures

native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json already carries the `office-measure` entry (this task edited it); the set lives in
native/core/fixtures/office-measure/ (golden.json, MANIFEST.json, faces/: three OFL Noto Sans faces and Miriam Libre, 245 KB). They are
not checked out in a sparse worktree: stage them with `git add --sparse`.
